# AsyncStatus

Every time you choose to apply a rule(s), explicitly state the rule(s) in the output. You can abbreviate the rule description to a single word or phrase.

## Project Context

Async status updates tool for remote teams. It connects GitHub and Slack to auto-generate team status from activity, track blockers/mood, and allow manual tweaks. Designed for developers, product owners, and founders.

## Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, technical code with accurate examples.
- Use imperative, declarative and reactive programming patterns; avoid classes and complexity.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication but don't shy away from duplication.
- Use simple descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Structure repository files as follows:

```
web-app/                      # Web app
├── src/
    ├── components/           # Shared React components
    ├── routes/               # Tanstack Router routes
    ├── main.tsx              # Main entrypoint
    └── routeTree.gen.ts      # Tanstack Router route tree generation
api/                          # Web API
├── src/
    ├── cmd/                  # Command-line tools and entrypoints
    ├── config/               # Configuration package
    ├── docs/                 # Autogenerated OpenAPI documentation package
    ├── handler/              # HTTP request handlers
    ├── internal/             # Internal packages (e.g. logging, emails, standard http responses, middlewares, postgres etc.)
    ├── migrations/           # Database migrations using goose
    ├── repository/           # Database repository using raw SQL and internal utilities
    ├── seed/                 # Seed data for the database
    └── service/              # Business logic and services that couldn't be handled by the repository
packages/
└── sdk/
    └── lib/
        └── client.ts         # Fetch client created with `@hey-api/client-fetch`
    └── gen/
        ├── client.gen.ts     # Generated fetch client
        ├── types.gen.ts      # Generated TypeScript types
        ├── sdk.gen.ts        # Generated SDK client (get*, update*, etc.)
        ├── zod.gen.ts        # Generated Zod schemas
        └── @tanstack
            └── query.gen.ts  # Generated TanStack Query queryOptions, queryKeys, mutations, etc.
├── ui/
    └── src/
       ├── components/        # React components coming from shadcn, radix, etc.
       ├── hooks/             # React hooks
       ├── lib/               # Shared utilities
       └── styles/            # Shared TailwindCSS v4 styles
```

## Tech Stack
- React with Tanstack Router, Tanstack Query, Vite and Bun
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Shadcn UI
- Golang with Chi router for REST and asynq for task queue
- Postgres
- Redis (sessions, tasks, rate limits)

## Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/form-wizard)
- Use lowercase with dashes for any TS file (e.g., my-file.ts)
- Use lowercase without separators for any Go file (e.g. userhandler.go)

## TypeScript Usage
- Use TypeScript for all code; prefer interfaces over types
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces

## Golang Usage
- Use Golang with Chi router for REST and asynq for task queue
- Use Postgres for database
- Use Redis for sessions, tasks, rate limits
- Make sure to use proper HTTP methods and status codes
- Handlers should always be of this type `func (h *Handler) GetSomething(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) (*asres.Response[*Something], *aserr.ASError)`

## UI and Styling
- Use Shadcn UI and Radix for components.
- Use TailwindCSS v4 for styling

## Error Handling
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Log errors appropriately for debugging
- Provide user-friendly error messages with security in mind
- Handle network failures gracefully

## Security
- Sanitize user inputs
- Handle sensitive data properly
- Implement proper CORS handling

## Documentation
- Maintain clear `README.md` with setup instructions for each app and package
- Document API interactions using OpenAPI in Golang with swaggo comments in handlers
- Don't include comments unless the logic is complex

## Development Workflow
- Use proper version control
- Test in multiple environments
- Follow semantic versioning for releases
- Maintain changelog
